Interpretation
  S41 refutes the S40 provisional 3p1/8 scalar target on the full B=13 bank.
  The full bank has 17 rows above 1/3 and 2 rows above 3/8, but no row above 2/5.
  The two 3/8 failures are low bounded rows with w=12 and strong even/dyadic packet structure.
  This points to either a 2p1/5 raw tax, or a split theorem:
    generic phase packets <=3p1/8, dyadic-even packet frontier <=2p1/5.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: dyadic_even_packet > phase_packet_concentration > p1_tax_constant > interval_envelope > endpoint_count
  observable: which carrier explains rows with Delta^+/p1 above 3/8
  switch/gauge: first sort by exact p1 ratio, then expose endpoint packets y=frac(w*x)
  Hamiltonian path: dyadic_even_packet > phase_packet_concentration > p1_tax_constant > interval_envelope > endpoint_count
  challenged assumption: after p1/3 failed, 3p1/8 looked viable in the sample; full B=13 shows
    a small dyadic-even frontier above 3/8, so constants must be stress-tested before canonization.
PASS: B=13 packet frontier complete.
